hadiths[42]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19043","Haddathana Abu Nuaym, haddathana Misar from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail who said: Haddathani my family from my father who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bucket of water, so he drank from it then spat in the bucket, then poured in the well - or: he drank from the bucket then spat in the well - so there emanated from it like the scent of musk."
"19044","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana Hajjaj from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prostrated placing his nose upon the ground."
"19045","Haddathana Abd al-Quddus ibn Bakr ibn Khunays who said: Anbaana al-Hajjaj from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail al-Hadrami from his father Wail ibn Hujr who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating upon his nose along with his forehead."
"19046","Haddathana Abd al-Quddus, akhbarana al-Hajjaj from Abd al-Jabbar from his father that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Amin."
"19047","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Sufyan from Salama ibn Kuhayl from Hujr ibn Anbas from Wail ibn Hujr who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite: nor of those astray, then say: Amin, prolonging his voice with it."
"19048","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman who said: And Shuba said: And he lowered his voice with it."
"19049","Haddathana Waki, haddathana al-Masudi from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail, haddathani my household from my father that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating between his palms."
"19050","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Sufyan from Asim ibn Kulayb from his father from Wail al-Hadrami that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prostrated, his hands close to his ears."
"19051","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Musa ibn Umayr al-Anbari from Alqama ibn Wail al-Hadrami from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his right upon his left in prayer."
"19052","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Sharik from Asim ibn Kulayb from Alqama ibn Wail ibn Hujr from his father who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in winter. He said: I saw his companions raising their hands in their garments."
"19053","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Shuba from Amr ibn Murra from Abi al-Bakhtari from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Yahsibi from Wail ibn Hujr al-Hadrami who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands with the takbir."
"19054","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Fitr from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands when he opened the prayer till his thumbs aligned with the lobes of his ears."
"19055","Haddathana Yunus ibn Muhammad, haddathana Abd al-Wahid, haddathana Asim ibn Kulayb from his father from Wail ibn Hujr al-Hadrami who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I shall surely look how he prays. He said: He faced the qibla, uttered takbir, and raised his hands till they were level with his shoulders. He said: Then he took his left with his right. He said: When he wanted to bow, he raised his hands till they were level with his shoulders. When he bowed, he placed his hands upon his knees. When he raised his head from bowing, he raised his hands till they were level with his shoulders. When he prostrated, he placed his hands in that place from his face. When he sat, he spread his left foot, placed his left hand upon his left knee, placed the edge of his right elbow upon his right thigh, contracted thirty and circled one, and pointed with his index finger."
"19056","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Misar who said: I heard Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail mentioning from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bucket of water, so he drank from it then spat."
"19057","Haddathana Waki from al-Masudi from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail, haddathani my household from my father that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands with the takbira, and placing his right upon his left in prayer."
"19058","Haddathana Waki, haddathana Shuba from Amr ibn Murra who said: I heard Aba al-Bakhtari al-Tai narrating from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Yahsibi from Wail ibn Hujr al-Hadrami that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he used to utter takbir when lowering and when rising, raise his hands at the takbir, and salute to his right and to his left. Shuba said: Aban, meaning Ibn Taghlib, said to me in the hadith: till the whiteness of his face appeared. So I said to Amr: Is in the hadith: till the whiteness of his face appeared? So Amr said: Or the like of that."
"19059","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jaafar, haddathana Shuba from Salama ibn Kuhayl from Hujr Abi al-Anbas who said: I heard Alqama narrating from Wail - or Hujr heard it from Wail - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer, and when he recited: not of those who earned anger, nor of those astray, he said: Amin, raising his voice with it. And he placed his right hand upon his left hand, and saluted to his right and to his left."
"19060","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jaafar, haddathana Shuba from Asim ibn Kulayb from his father from Wail al-Hadrami who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he uttered takbir when he entered, raised his hand, and when he wanted to bow raised his hands, and when he raised his head from bowing raised his hands, placed his palms, kept limbs away from the body, spread his left thigh from the right, and pointed with his index finger."
"19061","Haddathana Abu Muawiya, haddathana al-Hajjaj - and Yazid from al-Hajjaj - from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was - and Yazid said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - placing his nose upon the ground when he prostrated, along with his forehead."
"19062","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, haddathana Sufyan from Salama ibn Kuhayl from Hujr ibn Anbas from Wail ibn Hujr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to salute to his right and to his left."
"19063","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, akhbarana Sufyan from Asim ibn Kulayb from his father from Wail ibn Hujr who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he uttered takbir and raised his hands when he uttered takbir, meaning opening the prayer, and raised his hands when he uttered takbir, and raised his hands when he bowed, and raised his hands when he said: Allah hears him who praises Him, and prostrated and placed his hands level with his ears, then sat and spread his left foot, then placed his left hand upon his left knee, and placed his right forearm upon his right thigh, then pointed with his index, and placed the thumb upon the middle, and grasped the rest of his fingers, then prostrated, and his hands were level with his ears."
"19064","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, anbaana Israil from Simak ibn Harb from Alqama ibn Wail al-Hadrami from his father that a man called Suwayd ibn Tariq asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about wine, so he forbade him from it. He said: I make it as medicine. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a disease, not a medicine."
"19065","Haddathana Yahya ibn Adam, haddathana Israil from Abi Ishaq from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail from his father who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then a man said: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed therein. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed, he said: Who is the speaker? The man said: I, O Messenger of Allah, and I intended naught but good. So he said: Its gates of heaven were surely opened, and nothing held it back short of the Throne."
"19066","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana Ashath ibn Sawwar from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail ibn Hujr from his father who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was for me from his face that which I would not love to have for it the face of any man from the desert Arabs. I prayed behind him, and he used to raise his hands whenever he uttered takbir and raised and lowered, between the two prostrations, and salute to his right and to his left."
"19067","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Shuba from Simak from Alqama ibn Wail from his father that Tariq ibn Suwayd al-Jufi asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about wine, so he forbade him - or disliked for him - to make it. He said: We only make it as medicine. So he said: It is not a medicine, but it is a disease."
"19068","Haddathana Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik, akhbarana Abu Awana from Abd al-Malik from Alqama ibn Wail from Wail ibn Hujr who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when two men came disputing over land. One of them said: This one encroached upon my land, O Messenger of Allah, in the Jahiliyya - and he is Imru al-Qays ibn Abis al-Kindi, and his opponent Rabia ibn Abdan. So he said to him: Your proof. He said: I have no proof. He said: His oath. He said: Then he will go with it. He said: You have naught but that. He said: When he stood to swear, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cuts off land unjustly shall meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him."
"19069","Haddathana Abd al-Samad who said: Haddathana Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim, haddathana al-Amash from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail from his father who said: I saw the Messenger prostrating upon the ground, placing his forehead and his nose in his prostration."
"19070","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim who said: Thana Asim ibn Kulayb from his father from Wail ibn Hujr who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bow, placing his hands upon his knees."
"19071","Haddathana Affan who said: Thana Hammam, haddathana Muhammad ibn Juhada who said: Haddathani Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail from Alqama ibn Wail and a freedman of theirs that both of them narrated to him from his father Wail ibn Hujr that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands when he entered the prayer, uttering takbir - and Hammam described level with his ears - then wrapped himself in his garment, then placed his right hand upon his left. When he wanted to bow, he took his hands out of the garment, then raised them, uttered takbir, and bowed. When he said: Allah hears him who praises Him, he raised his hands. When he prostrated, he prostrated between his palms."
"19072","Haddathana Yahya ibn Adam and Abu Nuaym, both said: Thana Sufyan, haddathana Asim ibn Kulayb from his father from Wail ibn Hujr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prostrated placed his hands level with his ears."
"19073","Haddathana Yahya ibn Adam who said: Thana Sharik from Asim ibn Kulayb from his father from Wail ibn Hujr that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in prayer: Amin."
"19074","Haddathana Aswad ibn Amir, haddathana Sharik from Abi Ishaq from Alqama ibn Wail from his father who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his voice with Amin."
"19075","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Zaida, haddathana Asim ibn Kulayb, akhbarani my father that Wail ibn Hujr al-Hadrami informed him, saying: I said: I shall surely look at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) how he prays. He said: I looked at him: he stood, uttered takbir, and raised his hands till they aligned with his ears, then placed his right hand upon the back of his left palm, wrist and forearm. Then he said: When he wanted to bow, he raised his hands like them, and placed his hands upon his knees, then raised his head and raised his hands like them, then prostrated and placed his palms level with his ears, then sat and spread his left foot, placed his left palm upon his thigh and his left knee, and placed the edge of his right elbow upon his right thigh, then grasped between his fingers, made a circle, then raised his finger - I saw him moving it, supplicating with it. Then I came after that in a time in which there was cold, and I saw the people, with garments upon them, moving their hands beneath the garments from the cold."
"19076","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn al-Walid, haddathani Sufyan from Asim ibn Kulayb from his father from Wail ibn Hujr who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he uttered takbir raise his hands level with his ears, then when he bowed, then when he said: Allah hears him who praises Him, raise his hands. And I saw him holding his right upon his left in prayer. When he sat, he circled with the middle and the thumb, pointed with the index, placed his right hand upon his right thigh, and placed his left hand upon his left thigh."
"19077","Haddathana Mamar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi, haddathana al-Hajjaj from Abd al-Jabbar from his father who said: A woman was coerced in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he averted the hadd from her and established it upon the one who assaulted her, and he did not mention that he assigned for her a dowry."
"19078","Haddathana Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, haddathana Zuhayr, haddathana Abu Ishaq from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail from Wail who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his right hand upon his left in prayer, near the wrist, and placing his hand when making wajib till they both reach his ears, and I prayed behind him, and he recited: not of those who earned anger, nor of those astray, and said: Amin, raising his voice."
"19079","Haddathana Abu Ahmad, haddathana Misar from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bucket of Zamzam water, so he rinsed his mouth and spat into it, sweeter than musk - or he said: musk - and sniffed out water outside the bucket."
"19080","Haddathana Hasan ibn Musa, haddathana Zuhayr from Abi Ishaq from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing his right hand in prayer upon his left - then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Ibn Abi Bakr."
"19081","Haddathana Aswad ibn Amir, haddathana Zuhayr ibn Muawiya from Asim ibn Kulayb that his father informed him that Wail ibn Hujr informed him, saying: I said: I shall surely look at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) how he prays. So he stood and raised his hands till they aligned with his ears, then took his left with his right, then he said: When he wanted to bow, he raised his hands till they aligned with his ears, then placed his hands upon his knees, then raised and raised his hands like that, then prostrated and placed his hands level with his ears, then sat and spread his left foot, and placed his left palm upon his left knee - thigh in Asims description - then placed the edge of his right elbow upon his right thigh, and grasped three and made a circle, then I saw him saying thus - and Zuhayr pointed with his first index, grasped two fingers, and circled the thumb upon the second index."
"19082","Zuhayr said: Asim said: And Abd al-Jabbar narrated to me from some of his family that Wail said: I came to him another time, and upon the people were garments, in them cloaks with hoods and in them mantles, and I saw them saying thus beneath the garments."
"19083","Haddathana Hashim ibn al-Qasim, haddathana Shuba from Asim ibn Kulayb who said: I heard my father narrating from Wail al-Hadrami that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray: he uttered takbir and raised his hands; when he bowed raised his hands; when he raised his head from bowing raised his hands; kept arms away in his bowing and kept arms away in his prostration; when he sat for tashahhud he placed his right thigh upon the left, placed his right hand, pointed with his index finger, and circled with the middle."
"19084","Haddathana Aswad ibn Amir, haddathana Shuba from Asim ibn Kulayb who said: I heard my father narrating from Wail ibn Hujr al-Hadrami that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - then he mentioned it, saying therein: And he placed his right hand upon his left. He said: And Shuba added therein another time: When he was in bowing he placed his hand upon his knees and kept arms away in bowing."
